The MIT license above covers the code, schemas and documentation in this
repository. It does not cover:

- **Backbone weights.** A Flint checkpoint is a head trained on top of an
  encoder that someone else released. The encoder keeps its own upstream
  license, which `docs/model-card.md` and every published checkpoint record.
- **Checkpoints trained on data we cannot redistribute.** A checkpoint is only
  publishable when both the backbone and every corpus that produced its targets
  permit redistribution. `docs/training.md` spells out which corpora are safe
  and why; anything outside that list produces a checkpoint that stays local.
